; Names and blurbs for the guitars and finishes no disc names
; (content/hidden_guitars.h, gh1/guitars.h). Noah's to write: a token left ""
; is not added, and shows in game as its own name.
;
;   <key>              its name, on the guitar picker and in the store
;   <key>_desc         the picker's blurb
;   <key>_shop_desc    the store's blurb
;   <key>_locked_desc  the store's blurb while a guitar is still to be earned

; The Explorer's two unsold finishes (GH2's store).
(exp_peppermint "Peppermint")
(exp_peppermint_desc "")
(exp_peppermint_shop_desc "")
(exp_lipstick "Lipstick")
(exp_lipstick_desc "")
(exp_lipstick_shop_desc "")

; Nine of GH1's finishes that GH2's scenes still hold (GH2's store). Their
; blurbs are GH1's own (its locale.dta, by gibson_<body>_<finish>). Its names
; are the whole guitar's ("Goldtop Gibson Les Paul Standard"), where GH2
; names a finish under its guitar: each is GH1's cut down to how GH2's disc
; names that guitar's others, a Les Paul's by its model ("Cayenne Standard")
; and the rest's by colour ("Ice Blue Finish").
(lp_ebony "Ebony Standard")
(lp_ebony_desc "The all-time favorite Gibson model, the Les Paul Standard is recognized the world over as an icon for rock and roll.")
(lp_ebony_shop_desc "This classic Gibson Les Paul Standard comes in an Ebony finish.  It isn't fancy, but it rocks!")
(lp_gold "Goldtop Standard")
(lp_gold_desc "When the original Les Paul made its debut in 1952, the model featured a striking Goldtop finish. The Goldtop finish was originally offered from 1952-1958, returning in 1968 and still going strong today.")
(lp_gold_shop_desc "The Goldtop finish was originally offered from 1952-1958, returning in 1968 and still going strong today.")
(fb_copper "Copper Finish")
(fb_copper_desc "The top-of-the-line Firebird features mother-of-pearl fingerboard inlays that place it in the ranks of Gibson's most prestigious models.")
(fb_copper_shop_desc "This sleek copper finish compliments the unconventional shape of the Gibson Firebird.")
(fb_hippie "Psychedelic Finish")
(fb_hippie_desc "The Harmonix custom shop did the paint job on this Custom Gibson Firebird.  The inspiration was drawn from years of Friday night Led Zeppelin laser shows.")
(fb_hippie_shop_desc "Trade in your hard earned cash for this crazy cool custom finish on this Gibson Firebird.")
(mod_black "Ebony Finish")
(mod_black_desc "A bizarre mutation of the Flying V, the Moderne was designed in the 1950s but never went to market until the 1980s.")
(mod_black_shop_desc "Make a statement with the Gibson Moderne.  The post-modern design will get you noticed.")
(mod_dragon "Custom Dragon Finish")
(mod_dragon_desc "The Gibson Moderne's already innovative shape takes flight with the custom Night Dragon finish.  Only rock will soothe this savage beast!")
(mod_dragon_shop_desc "The Gibson Moderne's already innovative shape takes flight with the custom Night Dragon finish. Only rock can soothe this savage beast!")
(cor_white "White Finish")
(cor_white_desc "The mysterious shape of the Gibson Corvus attracted Xavier Stone at an early age.  One of his first guitars, it has accompanied him on more than 7 world tours.")
(cor_white_shop_desc "A classic take on a guitar that is anything but ordinary.  The Gibson Corvus.")
(cor_snake "Custom Snakeskin Finish")
(cor_snake_desc "Reptilian rockers love the Custom Snakeskin Gibson Corvus. Shed your conventional skin and slither your way into rock-stardom with this distinctive take on an already unique guitar.")
(cor_snake_shop_desc "A distinctive slant on an already unusual guitar, the Custom Snakeskin Gibson Corvus makes a memorable impression.")
(es_ebony "Ebony Finish")
(es_ebony_desc "\qES\q stands for Electric Spanish.  Typically, Spanish guitars are acoustic and have nylon strings.  The ES-335 brings a little something different to the world of rock electric guitar.")
(es_ebony_shop_desc "As classy as they come, you'll definitely raise some eyebrows playing this Ebony Gibson ES-335.")

